==Strategy==
Unlike in [[Envy's Flame Test]], this stage does have a difficult enemy combination with [[Metal|Metals]], essentially making it a [[Zero Legends]] version of [[March to Death (Merciless)|March to Death]].

The path to [[Marquis Clionius]] is blocked by the sheer amount of Metal enemies, and the [[Death Surge]] of [[Devil Wife|Devil Wife]] and [[Super Metal Hippoe]] serve to clear units from the blind spot if not countered. However, the slow speed of the boss means the support can be lured; simply allow the faster enemies to advance and fight them near the base before the boss arrives to reinforce them.

To give more time to kill the tricky enemies, the boss and the weaker initial support can be stalled at the base with units like [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]], [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]], and [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Future Cat]], taking care not to exhaust the money supply, then once the Super Metal Hippoe spawns he can be lured like normal, and damaged with [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critters]] including [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] and [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]], who serves the dual purpose of a [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercer]]. Once they are dead, it is mostly a matter of managing money and timing well, as unlike in March to Death, the boss has a blindspot, allowing the RNG aspect of Metals to be overcome by stacking as is standard.

